---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import Band from "../components/Band.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/ui/CtaBand.astro";
---
<Base title="HOA security, payments, and account access" description="How Common Parcel handles association payments, resident and board access, recorded approvals, and exports. Clear answers for your board’s review." path="/security">
  <Hero><p class="eyebrow">Money, access, and records</p><h1 class="t-display">Your board should know<br />how things work.</h1><p class="t-lede">Understand where payments go, who can access records, and how your association can take its records with it.</p></Hero>
  <section><div class="page"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Association payments</p><h2 class="t-sheet">Common Parcel does not hold HOA funds.</h2></div></div><p class="payment-intro">When online payments are enabled, owners pay through the association’s connected Stripe account. Stripe processes the payment and pays out to the association’s bank account.</p><ol class="payment-path"><li><span>01</span><h3>Resident pays</h3><p>Through the connected payment service.</p></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Stripe processes</h3><p>Under the association’s connected account.</p></li><li><span>03</span><h3>The association receives</h3><p>Payouts go to its own bank account.</p></li></ol></div></section>
  <Band title="Different roles, different access" field><dl class="roles"><div><dt>Residents</dt><dd>Access their approved lots, their own account information, and the association information shared with them.</dd></div><div><dt>Board officers</dt><dd>Work with association records and tasks according to their assigned roles.</dd></div><div><dt>Support staff</dt><dd>Use separate administrative access with its own access log. Support access does not make staff board officers.</dd></div></dl></Band>
  <Band title="Review before an important action"><p>Where a workflow requires a second officer’s approval, that review must be completed before proceeding. Common Parcel cannot sign for an officer, and support staff cannot supply the board’s approval.</p><p>Review the requirements for the specific action. A recorded approval is not proof that a legal notice was served.</p></Band>
  <Band title="A record of important activity" field><p>Approvals, exports, and administrative support access create records identifying the actor and the event. These records help the board review what happened.</p><p>The activity history does not represent a log of every ordinary page view.</p></Band>
  <Band title="Take your association’s records with you"><p>Board officers can export association records, including ledgers, governing documents, minutes, and available activity records. The archive includes a manifest showing record counts, completion status, and any errors encountered.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Ask a security or export question →</a><p class="small">For how information is handled, read our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p></Band>
  <CtaBand headline="Clear records for considered decisions." />
</Base>
<style>
  .payment-intro { max-width: 44em; margin-bottom: 36px; }.payment-path { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border: var(--stroke-edge); background: var(--field); }.payment-path li { padding: 32px; border-left: var(--stroke-edge); }.payment-path li:first-child { border-left: 0; }.payment-path span { font: 400 12px var(--font-mono); color: var(--terracotta); }.payment-path h3 { font: 450 23px/1.3 var(--font-serif); margin: 22px 0 14px; letter-spacing: -.035em; }.payment-path p { font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-3); margin: 0; }.roles { margin: 0; }.roles > div { border-top: var(--stroke-edge); padding-block: 20px; }.roles dt { font-weight: 600; }.roles dd { margin: 8px 0 0; color: var(--ink-2); }.small { font-size: 14px; } @media(max-width: 700px) { .payment-path { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.payment-path li { border-left: 0; border-top: var(--stroke-edge); }.payment-path li:first-child { border-top: 0; } }
</style>
